---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'About Free Audio Editor',
    url: 'https://freeaudioeditor.online/about',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="About Free Audio Editor — Local-First Online Audio Tools"
  description="Free Audio Editor is a suite of privacy-first audio tools that run entirely in your browser — no uploads, no signup, no watermarks."
  path="/about"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="container-page py-14">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-4xl">About</h1>
    <div class="mt-8 max-w-[70ch] space-y-6 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink2">
      <p>
        Free Audio Editor exists because editing a voice memo should not mean uploading
        it to somebody else's server. Every tool here — the
        <a href="/audio-trimmer" class="text-accent hover:underline">trimmer</a>,
        <a href="/mp3-cutter" class="text-accent hover:underline">cutter</a>,
        <a href="/audio-joiner" class="text-accent hover:underline">joiner</a> and the
        rest — runs the same way: your browser reads the file, edits it in memory, and
        writes the result straight back to your disk.
      </p>
      <p>
        That architecture is also why the tools are fast and free. There is no upload
        queue, no processing farm, and no storage bill — just your device doing the work
        it is already good at.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site is built as a static web app with the Web Audio API. It is actively
        developed, with converters, a voice recorder and more editing tools on the way.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
